# Normalize tracked text files to LF on checkin/checkout. Prevents CRLF
# from entering version control -- several of this repo's own frontmatter
# parsers are CRLF-blind (see scripts/tests/test_gitattributes_crlf_guard.py
# for the measured detail), so the safest posture is to never let CRLF land
# in the index in the first place, rather than trust every contributor's
# editor/OS/git config to agree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: exempt from the text/EOL normalization above. Both are
# PNGs and, like any compressed binary data, incidentally contain byte
# sequences that look like "\r\n" -- `text=auto`'s own binary heuristic
# would likely catch these anyway, but an explicit declaration is
# authoritative and doesn't depend on git's heuristic guessing right.
#
# scripts/tests/test_gitattributes_crlf_guard.py's real-repo guard trusts
# THIS file (via `git check-attr binary`), not a content sniff -- so any
# NEW binary asset added anywhere in this repo needs its own `binary` line
# here too, or that guard will false-positive on it (it will look like a
# CRLF violation when it is really just an unrelated binary byte pattern).
docs/logo/*.png binary
